# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# The immediate reason: `apps/web/node_modules` is a farm of pnpm symlinks
# pointing at a store outside the workspace. Copied into an image they become
# dangling links that shadow the modules `pnpm install` just created, and the
# web build failed with "Cannot find module next/dist/bin/next" -- from a
# directory where next had been installed seconds earlier.
#
# The standing reason: everything here is either generated, secret, or
# irrelevant to a build, and all of it is uploaded to the daemon on every
# `docker build` without this file.

**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

apps/web/.next
apps/web/playwright-report
apps/web/test-results

# Local state and anything that could carry a secret.
local-data
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.runner

# Documentation and scratch files change constantly and would bust the cache
# for a build that does not read them.
docs
*.md
!curriculum/**/*.md
!prompts/**/*.md
